<title>CANADA: Canada body details feed barley protein content.</title>
<headline>Canada body details feed barley protein content.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Canadian Grain Commission on Thursday detailed the protein content of Prairie feed barley.</p>
<p>	     Extra No1 Canada Western Feed Barley</p>
<p>PROVINCE   SAMPLES  MEAN AVG  MIN.  MAX.</p>
<p>Manitoba	92    11.8 pct  9.9   13.6</p>
<p>Sask.	  238    11.3 pct  8.6   14.5</p>
<p>Alberta	242    11.8 pct  8.3   16.1</p>
<p>W. Cnd.	572    11.6 pct  8.3   16.1</p>
<p>	     No1 Canada Western Feed Barley</p>
<p>PROVINCE   SAMPLES  MEAN AVG  MIN.  MAX.</p>
<p>Manitoba	28    11.9 pct  9.8   14.4</p>
<p>Sask.	   43    11.7 pct  9.6   15.1</p>
<p>Alberta	 65    11.8 pct  9.5   16.0</p>
<p>W. Cnd.	136    11.8 pct  9.5   16.0</p>
<p>	     No2 Canada Western Feed Barley</p>
<p>PROVINCE   SAMPLES  MEAN AVG  MIN.  MAX.</p>
<p>Manitoba	 4    12.4 pct 10.7   14.1</p>
<p>Sask.	   12    12.0 pct 10.8   14.2</p>
<p>Alberta	 29    12.2 pct 10.3   15.2</p>
<p>W. Cnd.	 45    12.2 pct 10.3   15.2</p>
<p>	     All Grades</p>
<p>PROVINCE   SAMPLES  MEAN AVG  MIN.  MAX.</p>
<p>Manitoba     124    11.8 pct  9.8   14.4</p>
<p>Sask.	  293    11.4 pct  8.6   15.1</p>
<p>Alberta	336    11.9 pct  8.3   16.1</p>
<p>W. Cnd.	753    11.7 pct  8.3   16.1</p>
<p>((Gilbert Le Gras 204 947 3548))</p>
